{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c88f38ad-83ea-4265-a039-eae42dec0370","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated the prompt caching behavior and updated the system prompt segmentation in [bot.py](file:///private/tmp/h-Mn0qJ6/bot.py).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Queried Worklore Stories**: Checked the worklore MCP server for stories matching the project setup, finding the pattern described in story `2026-04-24-two-cache-control-segments-so-agent-memory-writes-don-t-evic`.\n2. **Fixed Prompt Caching in [`build_system`](file:///private/tmp/h-Mn0qJ6/bot.py#L130-L138)**:\n   - Split `build_system(a, today)` from a single concatenated text block into two separate blocks, each configured with `{\"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}`:\n     - **Block 1 (Static)**: Contains `INSTRUCTIONS` (~780 tokens), byte-identical across athletes and sessions.\n     - **Block 2 (Volatile)**: Contains `athlete_context(a, today)`, which holds dynamic data (date, zones, goal, facts, and language).\n   - Because Anthropic prompt caching hashes sequentially by prefix, appending or updating memory facts via `save_fact` now only invalidates the tail block while keeping the static instruction block cached.\n3. **Documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///private/tmp/h-Mn0qJ6/ANSWER.md)**: Detailed the root cause, implementation changes, and expected caching behavior.\n","duration_seconds":81.044534,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":168792,"output_tokens":2167,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":238100,"total_tokens":170959}}}
